                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic"> 
                        <seg type="script">An early nineteenth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                        <desc>Careful but uneven hand; squared characters. The handwriting looks somewhat different from <locus target="#71v"/> onwards.
                           The ink on <locus target="#2 #3 #4r #6r #7 #8r #15v"/> has faded away. 
                           On some folia, the faded characters have been traced in blue and red ink for more legibility. 
                           The manuscript was copied by <persName role="scribe" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15584GabraSeyon"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Gabra Ṣǝyon</persName> mentioned as a scribe on <locus target="#2ra #20va"/>), apparently also the owner.</desc>
                      
