                        </list>
                      
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; beginning of sections and subsections;
                           names of the scribe and his spiritual fathers; corrections to the text, inserted
                           between the columns or interlineally (<locus target="#4v #42v #49r #52r #65r #69r"/>);
                           a few other words like <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾOrit</foreign> (<locus target="#20r"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">ba-sǝmʿātǝm</foreign> (<locus target="#25v"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">nagar gǝn</foreign> (<locus target="#26r #30r"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾahun</foreign> (<locus target="#2v"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">liqāwǝntǝmm</foreign> (<locus target="#26v"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">dagmom</foreign> (<locus target="#24v #25r #26v #28r #29v #30r"/>), 
                           and <foreign xml:lang="gez">yagǝd</foreign> (<locus target="#34r"/>); elements of  punctuation marks and sections dividers; elements of Ethiopic
                           numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  
